{number: 132}
{title: Glorious Things of Thee Are Spoken}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Glorious things of [F] thee are [C] spoken,
[G7] Zion, city [C] of our God;
He whose word can-[F] not be [C] broken
[G7] Formed thee for His [C] own abode:
On the [G7] Rock of [C] Ages founded,
[G7] What can shake thy [C] sure repose?
With sal-[C] vation's [F] walls sur-[C] rounded,
Thou may'st [G7] smile at all thy [C] foes.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] See, the streams of [F] living [C] waters,
[G7] Springing from e-[C] ternal love,
Well supply thy [F] sons and [C] daughters,
And [G7] all fear of [C] want remove:
Who can [G7] faint while [C] such a river
[G7] Ever flows their [C] thirst to assuage?
Grace which, [C] like the [F] Lord, the [C] Giver,
Never [G7] fails from age to [C] age.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Round each habi-[F] tation [C] hov'ring,
[G7] See the cloud and [C] fire appear
For a glory [F] and a [C] cov'ring,
[G7] Showing that the [C] Lord is near!
Glorious [G7] things of [C] thee are spoken,
[G7] Zion, city [C] of our God;
He whose [C] word can-[F] not be [C] broken
Formed thee [G7] for His own a-[C] bode.
{end_of_verse}
